{"availability":"available","full":"alkahest-cas/alkahest","name":"alkahest","description":"High-performance computer algebra system built for humans and AI","category":"Developer tools","language":"Rust","stars":17,"forks":0,"created":"2026-04-21T04:15:51Z","updated":"2026-10-11T06:21:00Z","license":"Apache-2.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://alkahest-cas.github.io/","topics":["agent-tools","computer-algebra","computer-algebra-system","python","rust"],"demo":"https://alkahest-cas.github.io/playground/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T07:26:13.140Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-11T07:26:13.140Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-11T07:26:13.140Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-11T07:26:13.140Z","stars":17,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Python","Rust"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Alkahest is a high-performance computer algebra system built for both humans and agents. It is especially well suited for autoresearch agents doing work in pure and applied mathematics. Available as a Python package or a Rust crate.","Alkahest is in beta. The API is still moving, and — despite the verification machinery described below — it will contain bugs, including answers that are wrong without saying so. Treat a result that matters as unverified until you have checked it: read the derivation log, export the Lean certificate where one is available, or cross-check against an independent source. tests/silenterrors/ measures how often the library returns a confident wrong answer rather than refusing; that rate is not zero for inputs nobody has tried yet. Please report what you find.","The main stack is: Rust kernel → FLINT/Arb (polynomials, ball arithmetic) → egglog + colored e-graphs (simplification) → Cranelift/LLVM JIT + MLIR (native and GPU codegen) → PyO3 → Python"],"features":["Verifiable by construction. Every computation produces a derivation log; a meaningful subset can export Lean 4 proofs for independent verification.","520× faster than SymPy on trig-identity simplification — and 77× faster than Mathematica on the same task (cross-CAS report).","40× faster than SymPy on 2-variable quadratic systems, via FLINT-backed polynomial arithmetic and a compiled F4 core (solving guide).","GPU codegen is a routine operation, not a research project — 16.2× over the CPU JIT on a 1M-point polynomial evaluation (NVPTX sm86, RTX 3090). Requires a source build with --features cuda; the PyPI wheel has no GPU…","A trained RL environment. GRPO against the CAS verifier moved Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct from 11.7% → 15.1% on elementary integrals (+29% relative) with no stored reference answers — the CAS grades every rollout, including…"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/alkahest-cas/alkahest/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"50f1a4ea33691669f88b4e5448cbf53c02f82c440febb7b76c02f71d6894c11a","extractedAt":"2026-10-11T07:26:13.238Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T07:26:13.238Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Alkahest is a high-performance computer algebra system built for both humans and agents. It is especially well suited for autoresearch agents doing work in pure and applied mathematics. Available as a Python package or a Rust crate.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/alkahest-cas/alkahest/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[{"text":"Alkahest is a high-performance computer algebra system built for both humans and agents. It is especially well suited for autoresearch agents doing work in pure and applied mathematics. Available as a Python package or a Rust crate.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/alkahest-cas/alkahest/blob/main/README.md"}],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"50f1a4ea33691669f88b4e5448cbf53c02f82c440febb7b76c02f71d6894c11a","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/alkahest-cas/alkahest/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-11T07:26:13.238Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-11T06:21:00Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/alkahest-cas/alkahest/blob/main/R